<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  Declares the Wi-Fi supplicant HAL, so that Android takes the AIDL path to it.

  WHY THIS FILE IS THE THING THAT SWITCHES THE PATH

  service-wifi.jar ships BOTH implementations, SupplicantStaIfaceHalAidlImpl and
  SupplicantStaIfaceHalHidlImpl, and chooses between them in
  SupplicantStaIfaceHal.initialize(), which asks
  SupplicantStaIfaceHalAidlImpl.serviceDeclared().  That is
  ServiceManager.isDeclared("android.hardware.wifi.supplicant.ISupplicant/default"),
  and isDeclared() reads the VINTF manifest.  It does NOT check whether anything
  has registered the service.  So registering waydroid-wifid's supplicant object
  without this file leaves Android taking the HIDL path to a HIDL service that
  does not exist, and the master toggle stays off exactly as it did in Stage 3.

  The instance name is "default", which with the interface name makes the
  registered service name ISupplicant/default: the string SUPPLICANT_SERVICE_NAME
  in wifi/Supplicant.h, and they have to agree.

  Version 1 is not a guess.  The frozen aidl_api snapshot this shim implements is
  android.hardware.wifi.supplicant version 1.  See docs/30-wifi-aidl-surface.md,
  finding 1.

  Same mechanism, same directory, as the widevine fragment in artifacts/widevine/,
  so this is a well trodden path on this host.

  Stage 4 of docs/29-wifi-plan.md.  Deployed to
  /var/lib/waydroid/overlay/vendor/etc/vintf/manifest/ and reversible by deleting
  it, but NOTE that adding or removing it needs
  "systemctl restart waydroid-container.service" rather than
  "waydroid container restart": the overlay is an overlayfs mount whose lowerdir
  is that directory, and files added to a mounted lowerdir are invisible.  See
  docs/32-wifi-stage3.md.

  One more trap, met while writing this file: an XML comment may not contain a
  double hyphen.  libvintf rejects the whole manifest if it does, and a rejected
  manifest declares nothing, which looks exactly like this file not being
  deployed at all.
-->
<manifest version="1.0" type="device">
    <hal format="aidl">
        <name>android.hardware.wifi.supplicant</name>
        <version>1</version>
        <fqname>ISupplicant/default</fqname>
    </hal>
</manifest>
